.TH PUTCHAR 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
putchar \- write one byte to standard output
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.BI "int putchar(int " character ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes the low byte of
.I character
to the Crunch standard output stream.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the written byte from 0 to 255, or
.B EOF
on error with
.B errno
and the stream error indicator set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fputc (3crunch),
.BR puts (3crunch),
.BR stdout (3crunch)
